;; Package clib hosts a C library inside a Python process (queue 208; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, "As built: 208";
;; PYS22 (a), doc/python/AFTER-PY11.md §1.7): the library and the part of musl 1.2.6 it reaches, built by ci's
;; builder into one node program (the library's package, e.g. arbace/clib/bzip2, holds it as text), loaded into a
;; program of its own (a ci.Prog over a crt address space) once per process, and called by the module's Go glue
;; (arbace/pybz2) function by function. The node program runs on one of ci's two back ends: interpreted by ci's
;; nodes (the Loader's code commands), or compiled, when the process links the library's cf2g package (pyi's AOT
;; does) and its init registered its setup (RegisterCompiled): cf2g's functions set as the Funcs' natives, the
;; data and static initializers the same text, so both lay memory out alike (doc/C23-SURVEY.md, CS120 (a)).
;;
;; The caller holds the GIL around every call: the library's program has one C thread (ci.Thread), which the
;; calls share. A C fault (SIGSEGV, SIGFPE) or exit inside the library ends the process as it would end
;; CPython's, with the fault's report on the standard error.
(in-ns 'go.arbace.clib) ^{:go/comments [[1 1 "// Package clib hosts a C library inside a Python process (queue 208; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"As built: 208\";"] [2 1 "// PYS22 (a), doc/python/AFTER-PY11.md §1.7): the library and the part of musl 1.2.6 it reaches, built by ci's"] [3 1 "// builder into one node program (the library's package, e.g. arbace/clib/bzip2, holds it as text), loaded into a"] [4 1 "// program of its own (a ci.Prog over a crt address space) once per process, and called by the module's Go glue"] [5 1 "// (arbace/pybz2) function by function. The node program runs on one of ci's two back ends: interpreted by ci's"] [6 1 "// nodes (the Loader's code commands), or compiled, when the process links the library's cf2g package (pyi's AOT"] [7 1 "// does) and its init registered its setup (RegisterCompiled): cf2g's functions set as the Funcs' natives, the"] [8 1 "// data and static initializers the same text, so both lay memory out alike (doc/C23-SURVEY.md, CS120 (a))."] [9 1 "//"] [10 1 "// The caller holds the GIL around every call: the library's program has one C thread (ci.Thread), which the"] [11 1 "// calls share. A C fault (SIGSEGV, SIGFPE) or exit inside the library ends the process as it would end"] [12 1 "// CPython's, with the fault's report on the standard error."] [24 1 "// Lib is one C library's program."] [30 2 "// Compiled tells whether cf2g's functions run (else ci's interpreter)."] [33 2 "// pending holds the calls the collector's cleanups queued (Defer), run before the next call."] [44 1 "// RegisterCompiled records the setup of a library's cf2g package (its init calls it): Open then loads the"] [45 1 "// library compiled."] [48 1 "// Open is the library name's program, made on the first call from its node program's text: loaded (or set"] [49 1 "// up compiled), its static initializers run, its read-only data sealed, then musl initialized as"] [50 1 "// __libc_start_main would (__init_libc: the thread pointer, the auxiliary vector) when the program links it."] [84 1 "// startStack lays out what __init_libc reads after the program's name, as ci's RunMain does for a program's"] [85 1 "// initial stack: the name, an empty environment and the auxiliary vector (AT_PAGESZ, AT_RANDOM); it gives"] [86 1 "// envp and the name's address."] [101 1 "// guard runs f, a C fault or exit inside it ending the process as C's would (128 + the signal, or exit's"] [102 1 "// status), the C thread's stack restored when f panics with anything else."] [125 1 "// Fn is the library's function name (a function of the node program, or a native musl's link left)."] [138 1 "// Call calls the function name with integer or pointer arguments and gives its integer result (the C"] [139 1 "// result's bits: the glue converts it to the C type, e.g. int32 for an int)."] [152 1 "// Malloc is musl's malloc(n) in the library's program; 0 when it fails."] [155 1 "// Free is musl's free(p)."] [162 1 "// Write copies b into the program's memory at p."] [169 1 "// Read is a copy of the n bytes at p."] [178 1 "// Load32, Store32, Load64 and Store64 read and write the program's memory (a C struct's fields)."] [184 1 "// Defer queues f to run on the library before its next call: a Python object's finalizer (runtime.SetFinalizer; goi has no AddCleanup, GOI-SPEC GC32),"] [185 1 "// which the collector runs on a goroutine of its own, without the GIL, frees the object's C memory this way."] [206 1 "// Realloc is realloc(p, n) for a block of old bytes: a new block, the old one's bytes copied, the old freed (so"] [207 1 "// the library's link needs only malloc and free); 0 when it fails, p then left as it was."]] :go/pos {:name [13 9] :package [13 1]} :go/semis [[54 24] [63 29] [75 34] [107 20]]} (go/file "clib.go" :doc "Package clib hosts a C library inside a Python process (queue 208; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"As built: 208\";\nPYS22 (a), doc/python/AFTER-PY11.md §1.7): the library and the part of musl 1.2.6 it reaches, built by ci's\nbuilder into one node program (the library's package, e.g. arbace/clib/bzip2, holds it as text), loaded into a\nprogram of its own (a ci.Prog over a crt address space) once per process, and called by the module's Go glue\n(arbace/pybz2) function by function. The node program runs on one of ci's two back ends: interpreted by ci's\nnodes (the Loader's code commands), or compiled, when the process links the library's cf2g package (pyi's AOT\ndoes) and its init registered its setup (RegisterCompiled): cf2g's functions set as the Funcs' natives, the\ndata and static initializers the same text, so both lay memory out alike (doc/C23-SURVEY.md, CS120 (a)).\n\nThe caller holds the GIL around every call: the library's program has one C thread (ci.Thread), which the\ncalls share. A C fault (SIGSEGV, SIGFPE) or exit inside the library ends the process as it would end\nCPython's, with the fault's report on the standard error.\n" :imports [


